    "    \"   \\\"source\\\": [\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"### Phase 9.3: Preprocess Data for LightGBM (Optional Demonstration)\\\\n\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"This section demonstrates **schema-driven preprocessing** using `preprocess_for_lightgbm()` from `finance_ml.ml_workflow.features`:\\\\n\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"- **Categorical Encoding**: Converts categorical columns to numeric via label encoding\\\\n\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"- **Datetime Feature Extraction**: Extracts temporal features using a consistent reference date\\\\n\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"- **Column Dropping**: Removes auxiliary columns not used for modeling\\\\n\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"- **Encoder Storage**: Returns encoders for inference-mode transformations\\\\n\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"**Note**: `prepare_classification_data()` already handles categorical encoding, so this step is typically **not needed** in the standard workflow. This demonstration is provided for reference when working with raw data directly.\\\\n\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\\n\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"**Best Practice**: Always store training encoders and feature column lists for consistent test/inference preprocessing (Section 1.3 of `code_guidelines.md`).\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   ],\\n\",\n",
